ps qualified for the Olympic demonstrations in Barcelona, with Argentine World Champions " [:a {:href "/athletes/900912"} "Fernando Abadía"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/900917"} "Fernando Elortondo"] " eager to add the Olympic title to their tally. Their team also included " [:a {:href "/athletes/900913"} "Ricardo Bizzozero"] ", the only Basque pelota player to appear in two Olympic Games. He had also competed in the paleta cuero demonstration of 1968. The Argentinians saw three close battles in the first round (40-38 versus France, 40-37 against Spain and 40-32 over Uruguay), had a relatively easy semi-final and beat Spain 40-30 in the final."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/900912"} "Fernando Abadía"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/900917"} "Fernando Elortondo"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/900913"} "Ricardo Bizzozero"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ARG"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ARG.png"}] "ARG"]] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/901288"} "Fernando Mendiluce"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/901250"} "Luis Altadill"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/901264"} "Pedro José Egaña"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/901305"} "Javier Juan Ubanell"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ESP"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ESP.png"}] "ESP"]] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/901399"} "Carlito Arenas"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/901408"} "Jean-Luc Cambos"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/901411"} "Christophe Casamajor"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/901443"} "Jean-Marc Petrissans"]] [:td {} [:a {:href